# The quality gates. NOT in core/Brewfile: nothing in lib/, bin/ or core/ runs
# any of these, so a machine that only uses the dotfiles must not carry them.
# core/Brewfile is machinery only -- see core/CLAUDE.md.
#
# Must stay in step with the install list in .github/workflows/ci.yml: a tool
# `make check` needs and CI omits is a suite that only runs where someone
# happened to have it. tests/contract.bats compares the two lists.
#
# Not enabling this module is fine; the Brewfile stands on its own:
#   brew bundle --file modules/dotfiles-dev/Brewfile

brew "bats-core"  # make test
brew "shellcheck" # make lint
brew "shfmt"      # make fmt, make fmt-check

# jq: json_parses in tests/helper.bash reads every shipped .json with it and
# has no skip guard, unlike the zsh and brew tests. Easy to miss, because macOS
# ships /usr/bin/jq from 15 on and MACOS_FLOOR is 14. claude-code names its own
# jq for runtime.
brew "jq"
